// is the FIRST user — the moment the legacy collapse ends — and only that
// create's response carries firstUserNotice (the spec's exact law: first
// creation announced, second creation silent). A duplicate username
// (identity normalizes lowercase before the UNIQUE check, so "Anna" and
// "anna" collide) is a 409.
//
// Self-service law: there is none to guard here — the admin group is the
// gate, and an admin may create any account including a second admin.
//
// @Summary     Create a user account
// @Tags        admin
// @ID          admin-users-create
// @Router      /admin/users [post]
// @Param       body body object true "{username, password}"
// @Success     201 {object} adminUserCreated "the created account; the FIRST user's response additionally carries the one-way-door notice"
// @Failure     400 {object} errorBody "malformed body, missing username or password"
// @Failure     401 {object} errorBody
// @Failure     403 {object} errorBody
